<.shell title="Navigation" current={:navigation}>
  <h1>Navigation</h1>
  <p class="lead">How people move between and within pages.</p>

  <h2>Top bar</h2>
  <p>
    Navy, with the amber rule and logo, as at the top of this page. It holds the team, the main
    sections, and the account menu. The current section is underlined in amber.
  </p>

  <h2>Breadcrumbs</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <ol class="breadcrumbs">
      <li><a href="#">Squamish SAR</a></li>
      <li><.svg_icon name="chevron-right" size={16} /><a href="#">Members</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page"><.svg_icon name="chevron-right" size={16} />Avery Chen</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    On every page below a section's list. The last item is the current page and is not a link.
  </p>

  <h2>Back link</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <a href="#" class="back-link"><.svg_icon name="chevron-left" size={16} />Settings</a>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    For pages outside the main tree, like a settings form, instead of breadcrumbs.
  </p>

  <h2>Tabs</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <nav class="tabs" aria-label="Member">
      <a href="#" aria-current="page">Attendance</a>
      <a href="#">Qualifications</a>
      <a href="#">Groups</a>
      <a href="#">ID card</a>
    </nav>
    <p>Each tab is its own page with its own URL, so links and the back button work.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Pagination</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="table-summary">
      <span>Showing 51 to 100 of 1,912 activities</span>
    </div>
    <nav aria-label="Pages">
      <ul class="pagination">
        <li><a href="#"><.svg_icon name="chevron-left" size={16} />Previous</a></li>
        <li><a href="#">1</a></li>
        <li><span aria-current="page">2</span></li>
        <li><a href="#">3</a></li>
        <li><span class="muted">…</span></li>
        <li><a href="#">39</a></li>
        <li><a href="#">Next<.svg_icon name="chevron-right" size={16} /></a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    Under long tables. Prefer filters that shrink the list over paging through it.
  </p>
</.shell>
